From a0098ed081d21ab1ae025695355d9e90eb738b72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yichao Yu <yyc1992@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:35:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] slsqp: replace the f2c core with a port of SciPy's
 BLAS/LAPACK-based C rewrite

Replace the f2c translation of Kraft's SLSQP (main iteration, LSQ, LSEI,
LSI, LDP, NNLS, LDL' update and the hand-written BLAS-1 loops) with a
port of SciPy's C rewrite of the same routines (scipy/scipy#22524),
which follows the same iterates but delegates the dense linear algebra
to BLAS/LAPACK (dgeqr2/dorm2r, dgerq2/dormr2, dgelsy, dtrsm, dtpmv, ...).
This cuts the time per iteration by 6-10x for a few hundred variables.

The NLopt wrapper and its stopping criteria are kept; the NLopt changes
of the old translation are carried over (bound clamping, backing off
from non-finite trial points, no iteration limit, gradient at the first
line-search trial point).  Unbounded variables are passed as NaN bounds
as in SciPy, and the DGELSY call marks all columns as fixed explicitly
instead of relying on stale workspace contents (same result as SciPy
after the first iteration, and about twice as fast as pivoted QR).

New algorithm parameters:
  linesearch_eager_grad (default 1, current behavior): evaluate the
    gradient at the first line-search trial point; 0 restores Kraft's
    function-only trial points.
  kraft_acc (default 0, current behavior): enables Kraft's own
    convergence tests with the given accuracy (SciPy's ftol).

NNLS includes a fix for an out-of-bounds write in SciPy's version when
the last column leaves the passive set (scipy/scipy#26561).

For now this links against an ILP64 BLAS/LAPACK with the "64_" suffix
(libblas64).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
