index d51fafd..021dbba 100644
--- a/src/algs/slsqp/README
+++ b/src/algs/slsqp/README
@@ -45,3 +45,33 @@ these kinds of algorithms), we plan to do so using a recursive call to
 NLopt.  (This will allow a user-specified line-search algorithm to be
 used, and will allow the gradient to be exploited in the exact line
 search, in contrast to the routine provided with SLSQP.)
+
+The f2c-translated algorithm (main iteration, LSQ, LSEI, LSI, LDP,
+NNLS and the LDL' update) was later replaced by a port of SciPy's C
+rewrite of the same routines (Ilhan Polat, scipy/scipy#22524), which
+keeps the algorithm and iterates but calls BLAS/LAPACK for the dense
+linear algebra, giving roughly an order of magnitude less time per
+iteration for problems with hundreds of variables.  SciPy's code is
+used with the NLopt modifications above carried over (bound clamping,
+backing off from non-finite trial points, no iteration limit) and two
+further changes: unbounded variables are passed to the subproblem as
+NaN bounds, as SciPy does, and the least-squares solve without
+inequality constraints marks all columns as fixed for DGELSY
+explicitly instead of relying on leftover workspace contents.  The
+code currently requires an ILP64 BLAS/LAPACK with the "64_" symbol
+suffix (see SLSQP_BLAS in slsqp.c).
+
+Two algorithm parameters (nlopt_set_param) control the remaining
+differences from the original algorithm:
+
+  linesearch_eager_grad (default 1): evaluate the gradient together with
+    the function at the first trial point of each line search, as
+    described above.  With 0, trial points are evaluated without
+    gradient and the gradient is evaluated once the step is accepted,
+    as in the original code.
+
+  kraft_acc (default 0): the ACC parameter of the original code, i.e.
+    SciPy's "ftol".  If positive, the original convergence tests
+    (predicted decrease, change in f or step length, and constraint
+    violation below kraft_acc) are used in addition to NLopt's own
+    stopping criteria; 0 disables them.
